Z||000038||BellaFiero||07-19-2000||10:29 AM||||If we're promoting Fieros here, then we are promoting making them run, keeping them running, and doing it with a bit of flair. THose gauges would certainly help in that effect. Whether or not you sit back and keep it to yourself, rest assured, we’ll figure it out on our own. I don’ t even care about a-pillar gauges ( too tacky for me ) I’ve installed the standard rally gauges from a 1988 GT and that suits me just fine. But the attitude of this thread semi-disgusts me! There aren’t ENOUGH FIEROS to be “Oh, I don’t want anyone else to look like me!” And I’ve yet to see ONE Fiero with the Mustang scoop addition, and I’ve lived in San Jose, California, Manhattan, New York, and St. Louis, MO as well as overseas ( my entire family is military ).  And I’ve yet to count five Fieros at any mall ( I’m guessing that comment was more for emphasis than anything else ). You think you won’t be original? You are original – you’re driving a commuter car turned sport’s car. I'm sure someone not affiliated with this board has the mustang scoop, the A-pillar gauges, the side scoops, the hood louvres, the over-the-roof scoops... Anything and everything we do to our cars, it’s been done and done better to some other make and model. Oh, I’ll be making the enemies today, but what the heck….  Why even post the picture?<p>[This message has been edited by BellaFiero (edited 07-19-2000).]||||reg||13
Z||000039||buds||07-19-2000||11:35 AM||||ya what he ^ said..||||reg||9
Z||000040||HYPTNOTiSE||07-19-2000||06:20 PM||||Don't imitate innovate.  I since i already have a rally gauge pod that came in my gt, thats where my volt and oil pressure gauges are, and since i spent good money to get white faces for those gauges, And since i needed a fuel pressure gauge(because i have nitrous, it always helps to have fuel pressure with nitrous <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">, and i need the gauge for tuning purposes) And i needed an air/fuel gauge for tuning purposes. I figured that an a-pillar gauge was better than having them hang by the wires or rolling around on the floor. And since i spend time dicking around finding a gauge pod that would fit as best as it could. After i spent money on buying an extra peice of a-pillar trim, after all of that stuff that anyone that posted on this thread could have done, BUT didn't. I'm supposed to give all that info out.  I thought that it would be cool to be different and be original, and i think that i deserved that, especially for the time that i spent. Guess not....<P>------------------<BR>Mike LeCompte<BR>86 Fiero GT 3.2L w/ nitrous||||reg||1
Z||000041||BellaFiero||07-19-2000||07:05 PM||||Wow... re-reading that, I came off like a real jerk. Sorry. I didn't mean it that way... Look, it is cool that you did that. And did it yourself. I'll bet it looks damned cool. But you did not explain WHY you did it. Only that you did it, and then when others asked how and what - you played a guessing game? Look, I'm glad you did it. Means it can be done. And for those who want it, they'll do it. Not my cup of tea, really. But I'm sure others have been lusting for an A-pillar gauge. I apologise. But still, when we see something new for our hobbies, we scramble until we get it. Not everyone has the mustang scoop. Not every owner lowers their car. But I didn't like the way it was held like "Ha Ha! Guess How!" in front of those who were interested in it. Just my nickel and you owe me three. ||||reg||7
Z||000042||HYPTNOTiSE||07-20-2000||09:03 AM||||Thanks for the understanding.  You're right i guess i shouldn't have played a guessing game, and i also found something else out from a friend of mine that has the worlds fastest all motor neon. The guy who sold me the pillar pod, just buys them from autometer and sells them to people!  So get one from carparts.com or something. It's for neons, the only one they sell for neons, not sure which years apply. You'll need to trim about 3/4 of an inch off the back side of the pod on the windsheild side for it to fit properly.  Also another reason why i didn't tell anyone is cos i figured i'd see a bunch of half ass attempts at just slapping em up there. So if you guys are gonna do it, do it right and take the time necessary. Thats all i ask. Don't mean to sound like a jerk,  but how many cars so you see with aftermarket shift knobs that are just sitting on top the stick not even secured.(not fieros in particular but all cars) And how many modifications to you see that are just rigged up. <P>------------------<BR>Mike LeCompte<BR>86 Fiero GT 3.2L w/ nitrous||||reg||1
Z||000043||Taijiguy||07-20-2000||01:23 PM||||Sadly Mike, there will ALWAYS be guys who will half-@$$ things. I have to admit, as I get closer and closer to painting my ride, I realize why it may be best to pay someone else to do it. It's easy to get excited, and be tempted to cut corners. God help me, I'm trying to stay calm and patient!<P>I feel it necessary to say also, that while seemingly under attack, you handled yourself with alot of style. I never noticed you getting po'd or lashing out.....very cool.<P>Taiji||||reg||1
Z||000044||BellaFiero||07-20-2000||02:55 PM||||Speaking of half-a@@ed work, I saw a Fiero and a Cavalier that had the "custom" Wal-Mart rims... you know, those shiny chrome-wanna-be hubcaps that press on over the fake disc brakes? Now aren't those cute? <BR>... <BR>Mike, how fast can you get your car up to with all the stuff you've done to it? Do you drive it on the street alot? ( Always thought nitrous would chew up an engine if used regularly ) ||||reg||12
Z||000045||HYPTNOTiSE||07-20-2000||06:33 PM||||Well, i'm kinda jumping the gun by saying i have a 3.2. I do, but unfortunately it's not installed yet. Getting the block o ringed, and re-balanced and all. So i can't give you actual numbers with my 3.2, but with my 2.8 which had everything available in bolt on parts, ported intakes, and tb, but stock cam and heads.  I have an 86 4 speed gt and i could get it to 105 in 3rd with nitrous at redline or a little after <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> that was probably around 6200 rpm. 4th who knows, but i was rolling. Never saw redline in 4th, but it was pegged on 125 for a while.  With nitrous i beat every car i raced on the street. If you wanna hear a nitrous success story talk to my man shaun hammit.  He's been running nitrous on his engine for a while and boy i'll tell you he isn't afraid to go under the sqeeze! He's a nitrous junky, like me. Shaun convinced me to get nitrous. I say get a wet kit that injects fuel and nitrous and get good ignition. Make sure your engine is tuned and tuned up and plugs are gapped properly. You'll be all good. Right now i'm working on a plate system, and I'm going to buy a progressive nitrous controller, so that i can spray 150shot, without the initial shot to the drivetrain, so i can ease it in and not spray 150 below 3500rpm. Shauns been running a 70 shot off idle for a while!<P>------------------<BR>Mike LeCompte<BR>86 Fiero GT 3.2L w/ nitrous||||reg||1
Z||000046||HYPTNOTiSE||07-20-2000||06:36 PM||||Well, i'm kinda jumping the gun by saying i have a 3.2. I do, but unfortunately it's not installed yet. Getting the block o ringed, and re-balanced and all. So i can't give you actual numbers with my 3.2, but with my 2.8 which had everything available in bolt on parts, ported intakes, and tb, but stock cam and heads.  I have an 86 4 speed gt and i could get it to 105 in 3rd with nitrous at redline or a little after <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> that was probably around 6200 rpm. 4th who knows, but i was rolling. Never saw redline in 4th, but it was pegged on 125 for a while.  With nitrous i beat every car i raced on the street. If you wanna hear a nitrous success story talk to my man shaun hammit.  He's been running nitrous on his engine for a while and boy i'll tell you he isn't afraid to go under the sqeeze! He's a nitrous junky, like me. Shaun convinced me to get nitrous. I say get a wet kit that injects fuel and nitrous and get good ignition. Make sure your engine is tuned and tuned up and plugs are gapped properly. You'll be all good. Right now i'm working on a plate system, and I'm going to buy a progressive nitrous controller, so that i can spray 150shot, without the initial shot to the drivetrain, so i can ease it in and not spray 150 below 3500rpm. Shauns been running a 70 shot off idle for a while!<P>------------------<BR>Mike LeCompte<BR>86 Fiero GT 3.2L w/ nitrous||||reg||1
